LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182405Z
UID:10006651-1783900800-1783987199@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Exploring Photography Without a Camera (Rising 9th – 12th grade)
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE \nPhotography doesn’t always require a camera. In this experimental image lab\, students will explore photography-based processes that use light\, chemistry\, and transfer techniques to create images. Through hands-on exploration of cyanotypes\, lumen prints\, pinhole photography\, and image transfers\, students will experiment with transparency\, layering\, and transformation—creating works that blur the line between photography\, printmaking\, and mixed media.     \nMeet the Instructor: Kristina Shriver\nKristina Shriver is a visual art educator with over 16 years of experience\, working with students of all ages. She teaches at Asheville High School and serves as an AP Studio Art Reader and mentor for other art educators. Kristina designs hands-on\, material-rich art experiences that connect historical techniques to contemporary practice\, emphasizing experimentation\, personal storytelling\, and meaningful creative exploration. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-exploring-photography-without-a-camera-rising-9th-12th-grade/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/SC2011.01.96.jpg
END:VEVENT
